message: "If you use this model or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "Kandy PM2.5 — a physically-structured decomposition model"
abstract: >-
  Hourly PM2.5 at 1 km over the Kandy basin, Sri Lanka (2019-2026), for a city
  with no public air-quality monitor. Concentration is decomposed into a regional
  and transboundary background plus a terrain-shaped local increment, combining a
  gradient-boosted temporal anchor with a road-network emission surface, terrain
  confinement and mass-consistent diagnostic winds, with conformal uncertainty and
  a population-exposure and health-burden layer. Because the target city cannot
  validate the result, the identical model is run at ten monitored analogue cities
  under the same two-sensor information budget and scored against withheld
  stations. Pre-registrations and an epistemic ledger are included.
